@resource-management.sigil from ResourceManagement import {
    Room,
    base availability rules,
}
@scheduling-and-recurrence.sigil from SchedulingAndRecurrence import { recurring booking series }

component Booking {
    goal {
        Create, confirm, and manage room bookings while preserving room availability,
        recurrence, and access boundaries.
    }

    interface {
        A renter starts a booking request for a Room and a requested time range.

        Before confirmation, Booking sends the Room and full requested range to
        Resource Management for an availability answer based on
        base availability rules.

        Booking requires a recurring booking series to confirm each occurrence of
        a repeated booking request.

        A confirmed booking records its Room, renter, requested time range, and
        confirmation status.

        A renter can cancel a confirmed booking that they own, subject to the
        cancellation rules.
    }

    state {
        Booking owns booking requests, confirmed bookings, and cancellation records.

        Booking exclusively owns the recurring booking series.

        A booking request can be pending, confirmed, rejected, or canceled.
    }

    logic {
        Booking checks the renter's permission through Identity and Access and asks
        Resource Management for the full-range availability answer for the Room.

        If permission is denied, Booking rejects the request and returns a rejection
        result that ends that path.

        If the availability answer denies the full range or a confirmed booking
        conflicts, Booking rejects the request and returns a rejection result that
        ends that path.

        For a single-time request, Booking confirms only when permission, availability,
        and conflict checks pass, then returns the confirmed booking and ends that
        path.

        For a repeated request, Booking uses the recurring booking series to identify
        each occurrence. It confirms the request only when permission, availability,
        and conflict checks pass for every occurrence, then returns the confirmed
        booking and ends that path.

        When a renter cancels a confirmed booking, Booking records the cancellation,
        preserves the booking history, returns the canceled booking, and ends that
        path.
    }

    constraints {
        Booking must not require a recurring booking series to confirm each
        occurrence of a repeated booking request.

        Booking owns conflicts with existing bookings and does not read Resource
        Management's private room data or availability logic.

        Identity and Access supplies current-user and permission checks. Booking does
        not own users, sessions, roles, or permission policy.

        Scheduling and Recurrence owns recurring booking patterns, series, and
        exceptions; Booking uses its public series contract for repeated requests.
    }

    cases {
        A renter requests a room for a range that fits its availability and has no
        conflicting booking; Booking confirms it when Identity and Access permits.

        A renter requests a range that overlaps an existing confirmed booking;
        Booking rejects the request.

        A renter cancels their confirmed booking; Booking records the cancellation
        and retains its history.
    }
}
